<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="58511" href="schedule/2011/fall/MCB/529/58511.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2011" href="schedule/2011.xml">2011</calendarYear><term id="120118" href="schedule/2011/fall.xml">Fall 2011</term><subject id="MCB" href="schedule/2011/fall/MCB.xml">Molecular and Cell Biology</subject><course id="529" href="schedule/2011/fall/MCB/529.xml">Special Topics Cell Devel Biol</course></parents><sectionNumber>PAO</sectionNumber><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Glycobiology  This course examines biosynthesis, properties, and biological roles of carbohydrate-containing molecules or glycans in animals, microbes, and plants. Topics include glycan analysis and enzymology, carbohydrate antigens, glycans in development, glycans in human and microbial disease, glycan synthesis as a drug target, glycans in biotechnology, and chemical glycobiology. Prerequisite: MCB 354 or consent of instructor.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2011-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2011-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1048</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Orlean" firstName="P">Orlean, P</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>